IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sarca-licensing`

-- Security and Related Activities (Control) Act 1996 (WA) with the Regulations 1997, ss 4A, 4B, 5, 11-16, 19-26, 42A, 49, 52-57, 60, 61, 67A, 72, 77, 77A, 79B, 80; regs 9, 16, 17, 25, Sch 1, 4, 5 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case. The Regulations 1997 were read from their deposit and their numbers are used.
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_security-and-related-activities-control-act-1996_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-jake and -daniel facts.json (Jake born 30 August
-- 2006). The scenario does not say whether Jake carries a baton, did the course or passed the examination; the fixture
-- ASSUMES no baton, course done, examination passed, licence decided 20 January 2034. His 2021 shop theft is plain
-- stealing (The Criminal Code s 378, not a special case), which is a Schedule 2 Division 2 offence.

§ `fixtures`

`Jake guarding the tower for Sentinel` MEANS `My work` WITH
    `I am paid for it` IS TRUE
    `I watch, guard or protect property` IS TRUE
    `my one employer, not a security agent, employs me to guard its own property` IS FALSE
    `I carry a firearm or baton while working` IS FALSE
    `I escort a person as a guard or protector` IS FALSE
    `I advise on watching, guarding or protecting property` IS FALSE
    `I install, maintain or repair security equipment listed in s 14` IS FALSE
    `the equipment is in a vehicle, vessel or aircraft` IS FALSE
    `as a regular duty I control, screen or remove people at a venue or event` IS FALSE
    `I investigate people's conduct or character, or look for missing persons` IS FALSE
    `I supply other people to do security work` IS FALSE
    `I am on official duty as a police officer or in the Defence Force` IS FALSE
    `I am on official duty as a public officer` IS FALSE
    `I am a court security, custodial or prison services contract worker doing that work` IS FALSE
    `I hold a temporary licence covering this work` IS FALSE

