§ `s 12 -- am I a security officer (k060, d04b)`

-- k060: guarding the tower for Sentinel, Jake is a security officer. d04b: had Jarrah employed its own unarmed guard,
-- that guard would not be one (s 12(2)); a baton brings him back in.
#ASSERT `Am I a security officer` `Jake guarding the tower for Sentinel`
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a security officer` `a guard employed by Jarrah to watch its own office`
#ASSERT `Am I a security officer` `an in-house guard who carries a baton`

§ `Parts 3-5 -- which licence the work needs`

#ASSERT `Does my work need this licence` `a security officer's licence` `Jake guarding the tower for Sentinel`
#ASSERT `Does my work need this licence` `a security bodyguard's licence` `a paid bodyguard`
#ASSERT `Does my work need this licence` `a security installer's licence` `a CCTV installer`
#ASSERT NOT `Does my work need this licence` `a security installer's licence` `a car alarm installer`
#ASSERT `Does my work need this licence` `an agent's licence` `Sentinel, placing officers at the tower`

§ `ss 16, 5, 42A, regs 5A, 5B -- may I work unlicensed (k060)`

-- k060: no. Jake may not stand a shift at the tower until his security officer's licence is issued.
#ASSERT NOT `May I do this work without a security officer's licence` `Jake guarding the tower for Sentinel`
#ASSERT `May I do this work without a security officer's licence` `a guard employed by Jarrah to watch its own office`
#ASSERT `May I do this work without a security officer's licence` `a police officer guarding a building on duty`

#ASSERT NOT `May I be employed as a security officer` FALSE

§ `ss 19, 15, 43 -- working for Sentinel (k060, d04b)`

#ASSERT `As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `As a licensed security officer, may I work on these terms` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE

-- d04b: the security contractor (Sentinel) supplies officers to the tower, so it needs a security agent's licence, held
-- for it by one of its officers (s 43(2)); not the ss 12-13 the scenario cites.
#ASSERT `Must the business I work for hold a security agent's licence` TRUE

§ `ss 23-26 -- firearms and batons`

#ASSERT `May I carry a baton while working` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I carry a baton while working` FALSE TRUE TRUE

#ASSERT `May I carry a firearm for this task` `escorting money or articles of value` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I carry a firearm for this task` `ordinary guarding of a building` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `May I carry a firearm for this task` `guarding money or valuables at a special occasion` TRUE FALSE TRUE

§ `ss 4A, 4B, reg 25 -- prohibited persons, spent and youth matters (k060)`

-- k060: the 2021 team referral is not a finding of guilt; no court acted.
#ASSERT NOT `Is this a finding of guilt` `Jake's 2021 shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team`
#ASSERT `Is this a finding of guilt` `the same theft, had a youth court found him guilty with no penalty`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this a finding of guilt` `a Division 1 conviction on 1 March 2028, quashed on appeal`

#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `Jake's 2021 shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `the same theft, had a youth court fined him $600` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `a Division 1 conviction on 1 March 2028` EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `a Division 1 conviction on 1 March 2028, spent` EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `a first Division 2 incident fined $300 in 2032` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `How many years does this matter disqualify me for` `a second Division 2 incident fined $200 in 2032` EQUALS 5

-- k060: even had a youth court found him guilty and fined him $600 in 2022, the 5 years ended on 1 March 2027.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a prohibited person because of it` `Jake's 2021 shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team` (Date 1 2 2034)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a prohibited person because of it` `the same theft, had a youth court fined him $600` (Date 1 2 2034)
#ASSERT `Am I a prohibited person because of it` `a Division 1 conviction on 1 March 2028` (Date 1 2 2034)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a prohibited person because of it` `a Division 1 conviction on 1 March 2028, spent` (Date 1 2 2034)
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a prohibited person because of it` `a Division 1 finding in June 1995` (Date 1 1 2000)

#ASSERT `Am I a prohibited person` (LIST `Jake's 2021 shop theft, sent to a juvenile justice team`, `a first Division 2 incident fined $600 in 2030`) (Date 1 2 2034)

§ `ss 52, 52A, 53, regs 16, 17 -- can I be issued a licence (k060)`

#ASSERT `Which training course must I complete` `a control-room monitor with no course` EQUALS `none is prescribed: monitoring duties only`

-- k060: on the assumed facts the officer may issue Jake's licence; his 2021 matter is no bar.
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `Jake's application, decided 20 January 2034` EQUALS `the officer may issue the licence`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `Jake applying at 17` EQUALS `not issued: I am under 18`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `an applicant with a 2028 Division 1 conviction` EQUALS `not issued: I am a prohibited person`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `an applicant with a disqualifying charge pending` EQUALS `not issued: a disqualifying charge is pending, without extenuating circumstances`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `an applicant exempted from the course` EQUALS `the officer may issue the licence`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `an applicant exempted from the course who seeks a baton endorsement` EQUALS `not issued: training not done`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `a control-room monitor with no course` EQUALS `the officer may issue the licence`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `a firearm endorsement applicant without the medical` EQUALS `not issued: medical examination not passed`
#ASSERT `Can I be issued a security officer's licence` `an applicant the officer finds not fit and proper` EQUALS `not issued: not of good character, or not fit and proper`

#ASSERT NOT `Was I given reasons for the refusal in time` (Date 1 3 2034) (Date 30 3 2034)

